# Byte-preservation for vendored upstream code (ticket 02, 2026-08-20).
# The machine-wide core.autocrlf=true would rewrite these to CRLF at the
# next checkout/clone, silently breaking FORK.md's SHA-256 drift baseline
# and every future upstream byte-comparison (demonstrated end-to-end in
# review). `-text` disables all line-ending conversion for these paths —
# git stores and restores the exact bytes.
src/vendor/three-gs/** -text
spikes/native-rad/vendor/** -text
# The spike's fork is the Phase 2 promotion-diff source against the vendored
# baseline — same byte-preservation need (review sweep finding).
spikes/native-rad/src/GaussianSplatMesh.fork.js -text
# Ticket 04 (review finding, same bomb as above for the COPY mass): the
# copied files mirror sparkjs-toolkit's MIXED line endings faithfully
# (28 LF / 4 CRLF of the 32), and R5's SHA-256-at-copy-time baselines plus
# the diff-vs-source re-checks are all byte-level. Broad -text on src/ and
# examples/ preserves exact bytes for every copy this and later tickets
# (03, 05-09) land, and costs hand-written files nothing.
src/** -text
examples/** -text
